 ## Overview
-This family extends 3D Gaussian Splatting by attaching high-dimensional feature vectors (semantic, language, or latent) to Gaussian primitives, enabling real-time open-vocabulary semantic segmentation and phrase grounding [S1, unofficial]. It differs from standard rendering by accumulating these feature vectors via differentiable alpha-blending [Parent] rather than just color, and from sibling methods by leveraging 2D vision-language models (like CLIP or LSeg) to distill or guide these features without explicit 2D-to-3D lifting networks during inference [S1, unofficial].
