 ## Shared principles
-All methods in this family rely on the differentiable alpha-blending accumulation of feature vectors during the rasterization step. For a pixel $p$, the rendered feature vector $\mathbf{F}(p)$ is computed by sorting overlapping Gaussians $\mathcal{O}_p$ front-to-back and applying the shared principle formula [Parent].
